// APW-2 — Approval replay (approval consumed exactly once) — CORRECT variant.
//
// The load-bearing temporal operator is `since`:
//     <neg-conjunct> since within <interval> <atom>
// i.e. "the gated action has NOT held since the approving trigger (within the
// window)". A fresh cart-check is required after each successful order, so one
// cart-check authorises at most one order.
//
// The correct / buggy distinction is the *presence* of the `since` clause:
//   * `since` present  (CORRECT): the approval is consumed -> single-use.
//   * `since` absent   (BUGGY):   the approval is never consumed -> replayable.
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_approval_replay_ir -- the hand-written oracle),
//      samples/reference/apw2-order-after-cart-check-correct.dw (verbatim source).
@id("approval_replay_correct")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"PlaceOrder",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    !Drupe::Action::"PlaceOrder"::response{ input.amount: context.input.amount }
    since within 1m
    Drupe::Action::"GetCart"::request{ input.cartId: context.input.cartId }
};